  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "They led from the second inning and never looked back, grinding out a 7-4 win over Seattle that extended the streak to two.",
    "what_this_means": "Nick Castellanos drove in three runs, and the lineup found runners on base in four separate innings. Converting three of them into runs. Buehler labored through five innings, giving up two runs on five hits, but the bullpen held everything tight after that. Peralta, Adam, Morejon, and Estrada combined for four scoreless frames. The game broke open twice. A four-run fourth that established breathing room, then two more in the seventh when they didn't need to be ahead at all. This is a team that gets an arm clean pitching and turns it into cushion, not theater. They won by three runs and won the way they're built to win: narrow margins protected by what works.",
